                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you think this game looks like hearthstone - you are not wrong: this small game is something like - Hearthstone *Singleplayer edition*. So, if you was looking for something similar but less competitive and frustrating that you can play from time to time - this game is great for you:\n\n+Visuals: the design of the hud, makes me think that this game originally was produced for tablets, it's not that bad, buttons big enough after all that's nice. Cartoonish monsters and characters as well as magic spells, all drawn pretty nice, so the game is quite relaxing from the visual point of view.\n+Gameplay: this game offers 3 packs of cards for your deck - offensive with monsters and attacking spells, defensive - with heals and protective spells, and magic - with tricks and devastating spells. You can stick to one or mix all of them. Simple casting spells mechanics - you should sacrifice cards to get more mana next round, so you can cast more cards or use higher value cards. To collect better cards you have an actual campaign with various quests, and a separate pack of quests that you can complete to get more gold for card boosters, or *shards* that can upgrade your cards. You can also destroy your cards to get more golds or shards (ofc better for shards).\n+Soundwork is okay\n+(Upd) - Now includes steam achievements\n+(Upd) - Now includes steam cards!\n\nBuggy cards selling process - fixed. \n\nAnyway - if you always wanted some single player game like hearthstone - this is a good and cheap solution.",
